sequenceDiagram
    participant Client as Client Application
    participant Server as NeMo Guardrails Server<br/>8000/TCP HTTP
    participant InputRails as Input Rails Pipeline<br/>(Colang + ML Models)
    participant LLM as LLM Provider<br/>443/TCP HTTPS TLS
    participant OutputRails as Output Rails Pipeline<br/>(Colang + ML Models)

    Note over Client,OutputRails: Flow 1: Guardrail-Mediated Chat Completion

    Client->>Server: POST /v1/chat/completions<br/>Auth: Bearer Token<br/>Body: messages[], config_id
    Server->>Server: Load/cache LLMRails<br/>for config_id
    Server->>InputRails: Evaluate input rails<br/>(jailbreak, topic, content)
    InputRails->>InputRails: Local ML inference<br/>(MiniLM, DeBERTa, spaCy)

    alt Input blocked by rails
        InputRails-->>Server: Rail violation detected
        Server-->>Client: 200 OK<br/>Blocked response message
    else Input passes rails
        InputRails-->>Server: Input approved
        Server->>LLM: POST /v1/chat/completions<br/>Auth: X-Authorization → Authorization<br/>TLS 1.2+
        LLM-->>Server: Chat completion response
        Server->>OutputRails: Evaluate output rails<br/>(fact-check, content filter)
        OutputRails->>OutputRails: Local ML inference<br/>(AlignScore, classifiers)

        alt Output blocked by rails
            OutputRails-->>Server: Rail violation detected
            Server-->>Client: 200 OK<br/>Filtered response message
        else Output passes rails
            OutputRails-->>Server: Output approved
            Server-->>Client: 200 OK<br/>LLM response (guardrail-verified)
        end
    end

    Note over Client,OutputRails: Flow 2: Standalone Guardrail Check

    Client->>Server: POST /v1/checks<br/>Body: messages[], config_id
    Server->>InputRails: Evaluate rails locally<br/>(no LLM call)
    InputRails->>InputRails: Colang rules +<br/>built-in model inference
    InputRails-->>Server: Rail evaluation results
    Server-->>Client: 200 OK<br/>Check results (pass/fail per rail)
